---
title: After (P10) - the request ends at 201; the email is held, published after COMMIT, sent by a worker
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Guest
  participant API as api.py reserve
  participant UoW as unit of work (main.py)
  participant BS as BookingService.reserve
  participant DB as SQLite / PostgreSQL
  participant Held as HeldConfirmations (this request)
  participant Q as QueuedNotificationSender (capacity 10)
  participant W as worker thread (HOTEL_WORKERS=1)
  participant Mail as EmailNotificationSender

  Guest->>API: POST /reservations
  API->>UoW: with unit_of_work() as service
  UoW->>BS: reserve(guest, room, stay)
  BS->>DB: has_overlap, next_reservation_id, INSERT
  BS->>Held: send_confirmation(Confirmation)
  Held->>Q: reserve(confirmation) - one attempt, never waits
  alt a place is free
    Q-->>Held: True (place held, counts against the bound)
    Held-->>BS: returns
    BS-->>UoW: Accepted, notification_failed=False
  else the queue is full or closing
    Q-->>Held: False, rejected += 1, status REJECTED, logged
    Held-->>BS: raises ConfirmationRefused
    BS-->>UoW: Accepted, notification_failed=True (R6: the booking is kept)
  end
  UoW->>DB: save_changes + COMMIT
  alt the COMMIT succeeded
    UoW->>Held: publish()
    Held->>Q: publish(confirmation) - put_nowait, accepted += 1, status QUEUED
  else the COMMIT failed (rollback)
    UoW->>Held: discard()
    Held->>Q: release(confirmation) - place given back, nothing sent
  end
  API-->>Guest: 201 Created in milliseconds, notificationFailed true or false
  Note over Q,Mail: away from the request - nobody is waiting
  W->>Q: get(timeout=0.05) - one job, status SENDING (in flight - neither queued nor completed)
  W->>Mail: send_confirmation (bounded by HOTEL_EMAIL_TIMEOUT)
  alt sent
    Mail-->>W: returns after 1 s
    W->>Q: completed += 1, status SENT
  else raised (after HOTEL_SEND_ATTEMPTS attempts, backoff between them)
    W->>Q: failed += 1, status FAILED, logged with the reservation id
  end
